course: dictionary
lesson: 8145
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Reproduce is a verb, and it has three main meanings. The words around it tell you which one to use. «Living things grow, use energy, reproduce and are made of cells» is a science sentence about life, so reproduce means to have babies, young, seeds or new cells.
explain: Reproduce can also mean to copy something exactly, like reproducing a picture. It can also mean to make something happen again in the same way. In science, «a fair test should be reproduced» so you can check your results. To choose the right meaning, ask what would fit, then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Be careful with clever machines. «Robots are not alive, though they can be very clever at tasks.» Being clever is not the same as being alive. Robots cannot reproduce, because only living things do.
fact: Reproduce is a verb: reproduce, reproduces, reproduced, reproducing.
fact: In science, to reproduce means that living things have babies, young, seeds or new cells.
fact: Plants reproduce with seeds, and animals reproduce with eggs or live young.
fact: To reproduce a picture means to copy it exactly.
fact: To reproduce an experiment means to make it happen again in the same way, so the results can be checked.
exercise: «Living things grow, use energy, reproduce and are made of cells.» What does reproduce mean here? | To stop growing | To copy something exactly | To make a loud noise | *To have babies, young, seeds or new cells
exercise: Priya wants to reproduce a drawing of a fox exactly. Which meaning is she using? | To make an experiment happen again | To break into pieces | To have young | *To copy something exactly
exercise: Choose the right verb form: Yesterday the plant ___ new seeds. | reproducing | *reproduced | reproduce | reproduces
test: A scientist wants to check her results, so she makes the experiment happen again in the same way. Which verb fits best? | Hide | *Reproduce | Throw away | Change
test: Which sentence uses reproduce to mean to have young? | *Rabbits can reproduce quickly in spring. | The teacher will reproduce the map on the board. | I will reproduce my favourite song on the piano.
exam: Which statement is true? | Robots reproduce whenever they are switched on | Robots reproduce with eggs, like birds | *Robots are not alive, so they cannot reproduce | Robots reproduce with seeds, like plants
